## How it builds the fix string and edit range (summary)

**Fix string:** The type arguments from each duplicate call are flattened (tuple operands have their elements spliced in, others contribute themselves). Source slices are obtained via the locator rather than re-rendered by the generator — the comment notes this avoids reformatting that could break things like f-strings with specific escape spellings. A trailing comma is appended when there's a single starred element. The final string is `format!("isinstance({target_src}, ({type_srcs}))")`.

**Edit range:** The replacement spans from the start of the first duplicate to the end of the last, using `parenthesized_range(...)` to absorb any wrapping parentheses (falling back to `.range()`). The result becomes a `TextRange::new(start, end)`, applied as an `unsafe_edit` with `pad(...)`.

